-## Example usage: Raspberry Pi 4, Raspberry Pi OS 64bit
-
-### Prepare image and configuration
-
-The following steps give a quick start using Raspbian. For a more detailed guide,
-especially concerning version compatibilities, please visit [the the corresponding thread](https://hub.mender.io/t/raspberry-pi-3-model-b-b-raspbian/140) on the Mender Hub.
-
-Download the raw Raspberry Pi disk image into a subdirectory input:
+Docker, a Linux host with loop device support, and the OTA-Pulse packages are needed.
 
 ```bash
-mkdir -p input
-cd input
-wget https://downloads.raspberrypi.com/raspios_lite_arm64/images/raspios_lite_arm64-2024-07-04/2024-07-04-raspios-bookworm-arm64-lite.img.xz
-```
-
-Extract the raw Raspberry Pi disk image:
-
-```bash
-xz --decompress 2024-07-04-raspios-bookworm-arm64-lite.img.xz
-INPUT_DISK_IMAGE=$(ls *raspios-bookworm*.img)
